inty, witness\\n97: existence or unjustified limit exchanges by notes. A familiar name or guessed\\n98: library availability is insufficient. A recorded note contains no unresolved\\n99: mathematical TODO. Do not log every associativity step or duplicate explicit M.\\n100: \\n101: Authors explicitly register important tools, write ordinary rigorous arguments\\n102: and self-check under this same policy; they need not anticipate every tiny M\\n103: use. An auditor can transparently complete routine accounting without returning\\n104: the whole NL0 for a rewrite. The accepted authority is immutable author NL0 plus\\n105: the hash-bound audit/notes supplement. It is not an old-policy claim that every\\n106: dependency was explicitly registered by the author.\\n107: \\n108: Fresh local reviewers may consult only logged read-only pinned-mathlib sources\\n109: in addition to their own packet and Yui rules. Preserve successful source probes\\n110: and actual tool readback evidence. This is\\n111: `fresh_packet_with_verified_background`, not old `fresh_packet_only` replay.\\n112: No other task, project proof, original/ancestor proof, repair history or owner\\n113: hint is permitted. Unverified facts remain FAIL/UNVERIFIED as appropriate.\\n114: Display PASS with background notes when present, retaining their count. The\\n115: supplement is mandatory translation input; none of its facts may become an\\n116: unproved Lean assumption. See [background notes](background-notes.md).\\n117: \\n118: A calculation label alone does not establish the existence of a canonical\\n119: decomposition, normal form, extremizer, basis or structural identification.\\n120: Give the actual construction and grounds for its required properties and\\n121: completion, or supply a verified source with its actual application. Before\\n122: declaring a mathematical obstruction, check the full quantified definition\\n123: and the direction of the claimed bounds. One feasible value alone does not\\n124: establish an extremal value. A failed attempted argument is not by itself\\n125: evidence against the supplied proof.\\n126: \\n127: Unfolding an explicitly supplied definition and displaying its logical\\n128: consequence is a local derivation; it does not need a separate source theorem\\n129: merely because that consequence has a familiar name. Conversely, a familiar\\n130: name without the required definition, premises and derivation supplies no\\n131: fact. Check the actual argument and identify the specific unsupported step;\\n132: do not replace that check with a blanket objection to a named result.\\n133: Distinguish a genuinely partial construction from an explicitly total\\n134: operation: its stated type/convention controls which existence guards are\\n135: needed, and totality alone grants no intended analytic property.\\n136: \\n137: Authors construct arguments and their evidence together, then report their\\n138: own actual check outcomes. An explicitly unresolved or unperformed check\\n139: prevents release as a complete artifact. Finishing a checklist, retrieving a\\n140: source, passing a structural gate or asserting that conditions hold proves\\n141: none of the mathematical requirements. Audit A remains an independent actual\\n142: judgment and can find an omission the author did not recognize.\\n143: <!-- yui-nl0-acceptance:end -->\\n144: \\n145: ## Auditor execution protocol\\n146: \\n147: The sections below implement the shared requirements. Reviewer identity,\\n148: fresh packet replay, negative controls, evidence capture and verdict handling\\n149: are auditor/controller duties; they are not extra mathematical facts for an\\n150: NL0 author. Mathematical FAIL findings identify the applicable shared table\\n151: ID and the exact unsupported implication. If the permission boundary itself\\n152: is ambiguous, disclose that ambiguity rather than silently raising the bar.\\n153: \\n154: Use [self-containment](self-containment.md) and the\\n155: [audit template](../templates/audit-a.md). New acceptance requires spec/graph\\n156: v2 and audit v3. Historical PASS records do not satisfy these requirements.\\n157: \\n158: This audit does not use a successful project Lean build as evidence that the\\n159: NL proof is correct. Querying pinned mathlib for source signatures is allowed;\\n160: reusing the target's historical Lean proof/verdict requires explicit disclosure\\n161: and does not establish an independent NL audit.\\n162: \\n163: ## A0. Freeze and disclose\\n164: \\n165: Read the original problem and independently check `spec.json`: target,\\n166: quantifiers, all H roots, parameter ranges, definitions, representatives,\\n167: normalization, endpoint conventions, and one-target scope. No H may originate\\n168: from the proof writer's desired conclusion. Audit target semantics, not just\\n169: hash equality. Record reviewer/carrier, shared context, read artifacts, and\\n170: whether any reference solution was seen. Read the canonical graph, not only\\n171: its generated Markdown. Bind the receipt to spec/graph hashes.\\n172: Generate the exhaustive global index with\\n173: `python3 nl0/scripts/nl0.py overview nl0.json --spec spec.json --out global-overview.json`.\\n174: It preserves every actual H (including unused or late-appended H), full global\\n175: statements/definitions and dependency edges with canonical pointers and hashes.\\n176: Read this inventory before claiming a node/condition is absent; a partial line\\n177: page cannot establish absence. The index supplies no verdict and does not\\n178: replace inspection of the relevant canonical proof and primary-source content.\\n179: The clean test adapter uses this same core generator, not a separate inventory\\n180: or mathematical standard.\\n181: Original-problem/source fidelity and local proof validity are separate tasks.\\n182: The original text may be read for target and citation checks; it may not fill\\n183: missing content during per-R packet-only replay. Record the actual boundary.\\n184: Check that original conditions really are H nodes, rather than predicates\\n185: hidden in a globally visible parameter type. A prime/nonzero condition,\\n186: characteristic constraint, range or equation must not become available to an\\n187: R with empty inputs through that encoding. Matching the full closed theorem\\n188: alone does not establish correct per-R H availability.\\n189: \\n190: ## A1. Definitions and notation\\n191: \\n192: For each D record a verdict with a concrete explanation. Check unique meaning,\\n193: type/domain, global versus local binding, definition dependencies, construction\\n194: or existence prerequisites, and applicability at every use. A guarded symbol\\n195: must not supply its own prerequisite. Record arbitrary choices, parameter\\n196: dependencies, and equivalence to the original definition. No project theorem\\n197: may hide as a definition, record field, predicate, or typeclass assumption.\\n198: \\n199: Reverse-check every actual mathematical object occurrence against a legitimate\\n200: declaration. Inspect local introduction position, first use, type/domain,\\n201: basis and end scope. Input-bound variables are not free locals; witnesses need\\n202: proved existence. Merely checking registered symbol names misses unregistered\\n203: ones. Definitions cannot smuggle properties or extra ancestor statements.\\n204: \\n205: ## A2. Sources\\n206: \\n207: For each M read the pinned official file and a successful full Lean signature\\n208: probe, not merely a `#check` name or a search result. Confirm declaration kind,\\n209: restatement, all implicit/typeclass assumptions, source hashes and commit,\\n210: relevant axioms, and suitability of scalar fields/domains. Library definitions\"}"}}

